 Sure, here's an example TypeScript script that uses axios, async/await to retrieve the file list from the provided URL and update the table:
```typescript
import axios from 'axios';

const url = 'https://kick.violass.club/files/';

const getFileList = async (): Promise<string[]> => {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(url);
    return response.data;
  } catch (error) {
    console.error(`Error retrieving file list: ${error}`);
    return [];
  }
};

const updateFileTable = async (fileList: string[]): Promise<void> => {
  console.log('Updating file table...');
  console.log('| File Name | Description |');
  console.log('| --- | --- |');
  for (const fileName of fileList) {
    const fileUrl = url + fileName;
    try {
      const response = await axios.head(fileUrl);
      const contentType = response.headers['content-type'];
      let description = '';
      if (contentType.startsWith('text/')) {
        description = 'This is an example text file.';
      } else if (contentType.startsWith('application/pdf')) {
        description = 'This is an example PDF document.';
      } else if (contentType.startsWith('image/')) {
        description = 'This is an example image file.';
      } else if (contentType.startsWith('text/csv')) {
        description = 'This is a sample data file in CSV format.';
      } else if (contentType.startsWith('video/')) {
        description = 'This is an example video file.';
      } else {
        description = 'This is an example file.';
      }
      console.log(`| ${fileName} | ${description} |`);
    } catch (error) {
      console.error(`Error retrieving file information for ${fileName}: ${error}`);
    }
  }
};

const main = async (): Promise<void> => {
  const fileList = await getFileList();
  await updateFileTable(fileList);
};

main();
```
This script first defines a function `getFileList` that retrieves the list of file names from the provided URL using axios. It then defines a function `updateFileTable` that takes the file list and updates the table with the file names and descriptions. The `updateFileTable` function uses axios to retrieve the content type of each file and sets the description based on the content type. Finally, the script defines a `main` function that calls `getFileList` and `updateFileTable` to update the table.

Note that this script assumes that the file names do not contain any special characters that need to be URL-encoded. If the file names may contain special characters, the script should URL-encode the file names before appending them to the URL.
